{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a thought-provoking film that delves into the fascinating story of facebook's creation and the tumultuous lives of its founders. directed by david fincher, the movie is a gripping narrative that explores the complexities of friendship, ambition, and the consequences of success.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a sophomore at harvard university, as he creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. this initial success sparks a chain of events that ultimately leads to the creation of facebook, a social networking site that quickly gains popularity among harvard students.\n\nas facebook's user base expands, mark is joined by his college roommates and fellow students eduardo savern, played by andrew garfield, and the winklevoss twins, played by armie hammer. however, the relationships between these characters are complicated, and the film expertly weaves together a complex narrative that explores the tensions and conflicts that arise as facebook's success grows.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its cinematography, which is sleek and modern, perfectly capturing the atmosphere of harvard university and the early days of the internet. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, adding to the film's tense and introspective mood.\n\nthe performances in the film are also noteworthy, with jesse eisenberg delivering a nuanced and captivating portrayal of mark zuckerberg. eisenberg's mark is a complex character, both brilliant and awkward, and he brings a depth and humanity to the role that is compelling to watch. andrew garfield is equally impressive as eduardo savern, bringing a sense of vulnerability and intensity to the character.\n\nthe film's exploration of the consequences of success is also thought-provoking. as facebook's user base grows, mark and his associates become embroiled in a series of lawsuits and conflicts that threaten to destroy their relationships and reputations. the film raises important questions about the nature of ambition, the costs of success, and the impact of technology on our lives.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that is both entertaining and intellectually stimulating. with its talented cast, impressive cinematography, and nuanced exploration of complex themes, it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people who created it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -1.1315475702285767}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0003067976504098624}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.01104797888547182}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " thought", "logprob": -1.8232431411743164}, {"token": "-prov", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oking", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0366092212498188}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0015041239093989134}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.3185122609138489}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -1.2993727978027891e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fascinating", "logprob": -0.615468442440033}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -0.0033919441048055887}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.004078404977917671}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.0009734659106470644}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " creation", "logprob": -0.13325300812721252}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.002492894185706973}, {"token": " tumult", "logprob": -0.6802005171775818}, {"token": "uous", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " lives", "logprob": -0.6084059476852417}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " its", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " founders", "lo